use /lib

export shape TableCollapsedRowsShape:
    description:
        A table that can collapse a run of rows at its start, and whose use
        says it does, shows in their place a first row reading "Show 1 …" or
        "Show N …", naming them, muted, beside a right chevron, with the rest
        of the rows beneath it.

    toggling:
        A single click on that row expands them in place, above the rest, and
        the row then reads "Hide 1 …" or "Hide N …" beside a down chevron;
        clicking it again collapses them. Each table is expanded or collapsed
        on its own.
